Z||000014||StuGood||11-07-2000||01:37 AM||||Coconut, letting you know you and yours are still in my prayers.  Hope you are hanging in there okay. ||||reg||3
Z||000015||Coconut||11-11-2000||03:19 PM||||O.K. gang, heres the latest scoop on my mom!<P>Mom had been in for Pancreatic surgery to remove a tumor that had eaten up about 2/3rds of her pancreas,(discovered by accident,by the way) she was admited for emergency surgery on Oct.31. Doctors had informed us that this was in fact a very delicate surgery and that she had a 1 in 3 chance of not making it off the table. All test could not confirm if the tumor was benign or malignant, but they had to work quickly to remove the tumor anyway and that the lab would be able to examine the tumor and give an accurate test result once the mass was extracted and submitted. VERY SCARY STUFF!<P>Surgery took 10 hrs. Talk about walking on pins and needles! Drove me bananas! After surgery was done, we spoke to the surgeon (he looked as if he had one TOUGH time, all red eyed and mentally exhausted)and he said there was a minor complication, but she pulled through.<P>Now back to where we were when I first originally posted....<P>Mom is doing well, the pnemonia has subsided and the heart attack she suffered as a result, did not cause any significant damage. She is now WIDE EYED and AWARE of her surroundings and just barely able to talk (she had been out since the operation, and until two days ago, did not show any signs of even being somewhat conscious. My heart lept for JOY when I saw her move her head, open her eyes, and faintly smile at us! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">! and after all she went through, she faintly asked..."Have you kids eaten yet?"(She loves to cook <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) Kristina softly kissed here forehead, my brother and I actually gave each other a big hug,(haven't done THAT in years) and all is good! We still have a long road ahead, but I can feel that she is on her way to recovery! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Forgive me for rambling on (I'm on such a high right now)! I just wanted to thank God and each and every one of you who took the time to focus on a little prayer for her. I firmly believe in "The Higher Power" God, Allah, Buddah, Jehova....to me, all these names are one and the same, and yes, He DOES listen....YA JUST GOTTA BELIEVE <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">!!!!<P>I know that God loves and listens to all his children, but I can't help but wonder (especially with how well my mother is doing now)......could he be paying a little more attention to the prayers of those that drive those neat little mid-engine cars that Pontiac made between '84 thru '88 <I>that HE likes</I>?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Food for thought!<P>Thanks for those prayers all, Coconut owes y'all a beer! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||7
Z||000016||hugh||11-11-2000||03:57 PM||||I tend to be emotional sometimes,this is one of those times.I wish you all the best.<BR>PS.  I think this coming Thanksgiving and Christmas will probably be your best.||||reg||1
