Z||000028||frontal lobe||11-15-2000||01:59 PM||||I am SO glad for you and your mother, because if it was pancreas CANCER, she would have only been with you here on earth for less than 3-6 months.<P>Congratulations to her surgeon, too, for a job well done.  Surgery on the pancreas is one of the technically most difficult of all--WAY harder than bypass surgery.  It's probably almost as hard as replacing the clutch in a Fiero!<P>She'll be weak for a while now, but should bounce back fine!  Great!||||reg||1
Z||000029||donny||11-16-2000||11:27 PM||||My family and I will keep you in our prayers.<BR>I hope and pray that everything continues to go good for your mother and your whole family.||||reg||1
Z||000030||Coconut||11-17-2000||03:27 PM||||Thanks Donny, I appreciate it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> BTW WELCOME ABOARD!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Hey Doc, yeah.... kinda plays with your head when one moment, a loved one seems just fine, and then suddenly, that life could be gone in an instant.....it's given me a whole new perspective in appreciating what we have on this earth now. Live, love, and learn as much as possible because if the Good Lord says it's your time, it would be a shame to have to leave feeling that we missed out on something  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ....that's what this experience has taught me! It's a lesson I will not soon forget!<BR>Cruisin' On,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by Coconut (edited 11-17-2000).]||||reg||14
